      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/centralia_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Centralia was laid out around 1850, amid Iowa's mid‑19th‑century territorial expansion for settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centralia%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1854, Centralia's lots surged from $25 to $200 as hopes grew it might become the first Dubuque & Pacific Railroad station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/centralia_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Centralia is part of the Dubuque, Iowa Metropolitan Statistical Area in eastern Iowa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centralia%2C_Iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Centralia began as the village of Dacotah, platted by William Stratton on January 23, 1851.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/centralia_iowa"
    },
    {
